	// Insight: For a given n, the number of divisors is small (at most a few thousand for n up to 10^12).
	// So we can iterate over all divisors D of n. For each divisor D, D represents a factor S(p,a).
	// Then we need to check if D can be written as 1+p+p^2+...+p^a for some prime p and a>=1.
